      "content": "That's a good start for the literature review. To get a bit more granular for the case studies, how do these differences in temperament manifest in terms of perceived volatility or emotional regulation? For instance, in a workplace crisis, would one group be more prone to avoidant conflict vs. more reactive/confrontational behaviors? I'm trying to see if there's a documented pattern regarding how \"predictable\" or \"unpredictable\" these stress responses are perceived to be in professional settings.",
